{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 40, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a film that tells the story of the founding of facebook and the subsequent lawsuits that followed. the movie begins with mark zuckerberg, played by jesse eisenberg, as a harvard undergraduate who is trying to find his place in the world. after being dumped by his girlfriend, erica, mark creates a website called facemash, which allows users to compare the photos of two students and vote on which one is more attractive.\n\nthe site becomes a huge success, but also generates a lot of controversy and gets mark into trouble with the university. however, it also catches the attention of twin brothers cameron and tyler winklevoss, who approach mark with an idea for a social networking site exclusively for harvard students. mark agrees to work on the project, but soon drops the twins and starts working on his own site, which eventually becomes facebook.\n\nthe film then follows the rapid growth of facebook, as well as the legal battles that mark faces with the winklevoss twins, who claim that mark stole their idea. the movie also explores the relationship between mark and his best friend and co-founder, eduardo saverin, who becomes increasingly frustrated with mark's actions and eventually gets pushed out of the company.\n\none of the strengths of the movie is its script, which was written by aaron sorkin. the dialogue is witty and engaging, and the characters are well-developed and complex. the film also features a talented cast, including andrew garfield as eduardo saverin and justin timberlake as sean parker, the co-founder of napster who becomes a key player in facebook's early days.\n\nthe movie's portrayal of mark zuckerberg has been somewhat controversial, with some people feeling that it is unfair and inaccurate. however, it is worth noting that the film is based on a book called \"the accidental billionaires\" by ben mezrich, w